# Edit this file to introduce tasks to be run by cron.
#
# Each task to run has to be defined through a single line
# indicating with different fields when the task will be run
# and what command to run for the task
#
# To define the time you can provide concrete values for
# minute (m), hour (h), day of month (dom), month (mon),
# and day of week (dow) or use '*' in these fields (for 'any').
#
# Notice that tasks will be started based on the cron's system
# daemon's notion of time and timezones.
#
# Output of the crontab jobs (including errors) is sent through
# email to the user the crontab file belongs to (unless redirected).
#
# For example, you can run a backup of all your user accounts
# at 5 a.m every week with:
# 0 5 * * 1 tar -zcf /var/backups/home.tgz /home/
#
# For more information see the manual pages of crontab(5) and cron(8)
#
# m h  dom mon dow   command

# N.B. All times are UTC. Ada's OpenClaw crons run at 7:45–8:00 AM UTC (3:45–4:00 AM ET).
#      Root scripts at 7:25 and 7:30 must complete before Ada's crons start.
#
# ORDERING MATTERS for the daily-brief staging directories:
#   7:25 — pre-create runs/DATE and fragments/DATE as openclaw (MUST run before 7:30 scripts)
#   7:30 — all data-fetch scripts run concurrently; they write into the pre-created dir

# [7:25] Pre-create today's brief runs + fragments directories as openclaw.
# Guarantees both daily-brief staging directories are openclaw-owned before
# any 7:30 script touches them.
25 7 * * * bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/cron/prepare-daily-brief-paths.sh

# [7:29] sls-system: audit workspace file protection (chattr +i) before security checks run.
# Reads the immutable bit on all protected skill/identity files via lsattr (no root needed).
# Writes working/sls-system/immutable-check.json; merged into security checks by build.py at 7:45.
29 7 * * * bash /opt/protect-workspace.sh check-reset >> /var/log/sls-immutable-check.log 2>&1

# [7:30] sls-system: run security audit and system health checks as root.
# Writes working/sls-system/security.json and health.json.
# Ada's sls-system cron (7:45 AM UTC) reads these files to build the brief fragment.
30 7 * * * mkdir -p /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-system && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-system/scripts/security-audit.sh > /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-system/security.json 2>&1 && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-system/scripts/system-health.sh > /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-system/health.json 2>&1

# [7:30] sls-openclaw: run OpenClaw gateway health check as root.
# Writes working/sls-openclaw/health.json.
# Ada's sls-openclaw cron (7:47 AM UTC) reads this file to build the brief fragment.
30 7 * * * mkdir -p /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-openclaw && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-openclaw/scripts/openclaw-health.sh > /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-openclaw/health.json 2>/home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-openclaw/health.err

# [7:30] sls-calendar: collect Google Calendar data outside the model sandbox.
# The wrapper runs the fetcher as openclaw so refreshed OAuth tokens and output
# artifacts retain openclaw ownership. The 7:53 agent only verifies the result.
30 7 * * * mkdir -p /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-calendar && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-calendar/scripts/fetch-calendar-host.sh >> /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-calendar/fetch-calendar.log 2>&1

# [7:30] sls-costs: fetch AI provider cost data from Anthropic, GitHub, Google Cloud, and DigitalOcean APIs.
# Reads ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN, DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN, GOOGLE_BILLING_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY from /opt/openclaw.env.
# Writes working/sls-costs/YYYY-MM-DD.json.
# Ada's sls-costs cron (7:58 AM UTC) reads this artifact to render the "AI Costs" brief section.
30 7 * * * bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-costs/scripts/fetch-costs.sh

# [7:30] sls-news-gemini: fetch daily news via Gemini API with grounding.
# Reads GEMINI_API_KEY from /opt/openclaw.env.
# Writes news-*.html fragments to fragments/DATE/. Ada cron for this skill is disabled;
# sls-daily-brief assembler reads these fragments directly.
30 7 * * * mkdir -p /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-news-gemini && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-news-gemini/scripts/fetch-news.sh >> /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-news-gemini/fetch-news.log 2>&1

# [7:30] sls-inbox: fetch Ada's inbox via himalaya IMAP as root.
# Reads HIMALAYA_PASSWORD from /opt/openclaw.env.
# Exports all 24h envelopes and message parts to working/sls-inbox/himalaya-run/.
# Ada's sls-inbox cron (7:55 AM UTC) reads pre-fetched data; makes no live IMAP calls.
30 7 * * * bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-inbox/scripts/fetch-inbox.sh >> /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-inbox/fetch-inbox.log 2>&1

# [7:32] sls-inbox heroes: fetch OG hero images for newsletter toc cards.
# Runs 2 minutes after fetch-inbox.sh so envelope exports are ready.
# Reads the pre-fetched envelopes/exports, fetches og:image from each source's
# canonical web URL, downloads the image, and writes:
#   working/sls-inbox/heroes-DATE.json  (per-source outcome manifest)
#   public/assets/images/newsletter-heroes/DATE-<slug>.<ext>  (images, git-ignored)
# Ada's sls-inbox cron reads the manifest offline; missing manifest = no hero banners.
32 7 * * * runuser -u openclaw -- env OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE=/home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace python3 /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-inbox/scripts/fetch_heroes.py >> /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-inbox/fetch-heroes.log 2>&1

# [7:30] sls-images: fetch Unsplash photos for the gallery section of the daily brief.
# Reads UNSPLASH_API_KEY from /opt/openclaw.env.
# Writes fragments/DATE/sls-images.html.
# Ada's sls-images cron (7:57 AM UTC) verifies this fragment exists.
30 7 * * * mkdir -p /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-images && bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/.agents/skills/sls-images/scripts/fetch-images.sh >> /home/openclaw/.openclaw/workspace/working/sls-images/fetch-images.log 2>&1

# [7:35] workspace prune: delete accumulated session artifacts and enforce shell-snapshot permissions.
# Covers: sandbox/skills-workspaces (3d), sls-daily-brief fragments/runs/security-audits (14d),
# sls-calendar (14d), telegram session dirs (14d), sls-alerts delivery receipts (14d),
# and Codex shell snapshots (700/600 enforcement + 3d prune with JSONL audit trail).
# Runs after the 7:30 fetch wave so nothing written today is touched.
# Edit cron/prune-workspace.sh to adjust targets or retention — no crontab change needed.
35 7 * * * bash /home/openclaw/.openclaw/cron/prune-workspace.sh >> /var/log/sls-workspace-prune.log 2>&1
